  "details": "Other player's avatars with parent constrained items don't scale correctly when they change size.\n\n1. Get a friend to wear an avatar with say, a 'snout indicator', a small object parent constrained to the head to show to the local player where the tip of their character's nose is.\n\n2. Have that player adjust their scaling to non-base size.\n\n3. The object that forms the snout indicator changes size but does not change its relative distance away from them, meaning it becomes visible as it exits the head mesh it should be hidden inside of.",
